WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
Chapter four. What the toolkit costs.

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.020
There are seven tools in this chapter.

3
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:07.760
You need about two of them.

4
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.620
Everyone converged on twenty dollars a month,

5
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.740
because that happens to be the number people

6
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.320
pay without thinking about it.

7
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.780
The free tiers have become genuinely good,

8
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:19.020
which complicates the picture in a useful

9
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.600
way. Let me go through what each one is for.

10
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.740
ChatGPT is the broadest.

11
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.220
Biggest feature set,

12
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.300
biggest ecosystem, and a free tier that now

13
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.120
carries ads. Claude handles long documents

14
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.220
and careful reasoning,

15
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.580
and Claude Code comes included from twenty

16
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.060
dollars. If you want to build things,

17
00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:40.460
that is the cheapest serious setup available.

18
00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.820
Perplexity is an answer engine.

19
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.560
It searches the live web,

20
00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:45.840
reads what it finds,

21
00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:48.540
and puts a citation on every claim so you

22
00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.560
can check it. If you are a student,

23
00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.880
Education Pro is ten dollars instead of twenty,

24
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.960
verified with an academic email,

25
00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:57.840
and almost nobody claims it.

26
00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.920
Gemini lives inside Gmail and Docs and Drive,

27
00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.060
and copes well with very long inputs.

28
00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.780
Gemini Notebook, which was called NotebookLM

29
00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.700
until July, only answers from sources you

30
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.120
upload. That restriction is the whole feature.

31
00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:13.460
It cannot wander into half-remembered training

32
00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:15.340
data, because it has nothing else to draw

33
00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.140
on. Gamma builds a first-draft deck from a

34
00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:18.140
prompt in about two minutes.

35
00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.800
And Higgsfield generates video and images.

36
00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:22.420
Now, the part worth remembering.

37
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.380
The two-hundred-dollar plans from ChatGPT

38
00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.160
and Claude are both metered,

39
00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:27.340
so even those run out.

40
00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:31.960
Claude Max mostly buys you headroom,

41
00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:33.080
plus Fable inside the plan.

42
00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:34.640
If you are not hitting your limits,

43
00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:35.680
you do not need it yet.

44
00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.080
Prices change all the time,

45
00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.600
so check them before you quote me on any of

46
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.200
this.

